+/**
+ * Keeps a dictation transcript with the composer it was started in.
+ *
+ * One composer stays mounted across session switches, and a transcript only
+ * arrives after the recording is confirmed and transcribed. A switch inside
+ * that window used to insert — or send — the transcript in whichever session
+ * was on screen when it landed. The origin is recorded when recording starts;
+ * a transcript whose origin is no longer the rendered composer is appended to
+ * the origin's draft instead and never reaches the visible composer.
+ *
+ * "The composer" is not the draft identity: a new-session draft keeps its
+ * identity across a project, worktree or Chat/Project switch only by moving
+ * directory, and the composer carries typed text along with that move. The
+ * origin is therefore keyed by the composer's stable key (its session, or the
+ * open draft's id), and only the draft identity is used as the place to store
+ * a transcript that genuinely belongs elsewhere.
+ */
 
